 "# name: ra-inv-one-add-div-pow-limit-test\n# technique: test a claim no recipe certifies, at instances Sage evaluates exactly or by intervals\n# goal: sage_test KaluzaKlein.RealAnalysis.Series.inv_one_add_div_pow_limit file \"ra-inv-one-add-div-pow-limit-test.sage\"\n# description: Sage's limit of 1/(1 + x/n)^n is e^(-x); at x = 1, (n/(n+1))^n → 1/e\nSEED = 0  # the instances are listed, no sampling\nR = RealIntervalField(128)\ndef B(b):\n    return QQ(1 if bool(b) else 0)\nRI = RealIntervalField(256)\ndef O(values, lhs, rhs, rel='==', edge=False):\n    # symbolic values (π, e, logs, limits Sage computed) are compared by 256-bit intervals; rationals exactly\n    if any(hasattr(v, 'parent') and v.parent() is SR for v in (lhs, rhs)):\n        lhs, rhs = RI(lhs), RI(rhs)\n    return oracle_instance(*values, lhs=lhs, rhs=rhs, relation=rel, edge=edge)\nn = var('n')\ninstances = [O([str(v)], limit(1 / (1 + v / n) ** n, n=oo), exp(-v), edge=(v == 0)) for v in [0, 1, 2, -1]]\n",
